From bd2e949c4b9333ae1404779121ba97040dee3d39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adhemerval Zanella <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:57:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 78/80] UPSTREAM: posix: Fix double free after allocation
 failure in regcomp and regexec (BZ 34991, CVE-2026-100290)

The re_dfa_add_node and build_range_exp grow paired arrays with consecutive
reallocs and store the results only after all of them succeed.  If a
later realloc fails, the structure keeps pointers to freed blocks, and
the cleanup frees them again (BZ 31935).  Store each result as soon as
its realloc succeeds, as gnulib commit 9db7e04d15 did for
re_dfa_add_node.

Also, the match_ctx_add_entry frees bkref_ents when growing it fails but
keeps thepointer, so match_ctx_free frees it again.  Keep the old array
instead.

The tst-regcomp-bracket-free now also covers the re_dfa_add_node and
build_range_exp paths.

Checked on x86_64-linux-gnu and i686-linux-gnu.

(cherry picked from commit 2a605083deb2c26e93b3be9943f5139e932c9f96)
---
 posix/Makefile                   |   1 +
 posix/regcomp.c                  |  18 +--
 posix/regex_internal.c           |  22 ++--
 posix/regexec.c                  |   5 +-
 posix/tst-regcomp-bracket-free.c | 215 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 5 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

diff --git a/posix/Makefile b/posix/Makefile
index 7478cc2174..e3a24c6a85 100644
